### Page 1 of 2

```text
Approved ato
CONTRACT NO.
Date:
CONTRACT EMPLOYMENT AGREEMENT
THIS AGREEMENT, made and entered into this — day of August, 2019, by and between
the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, a municipal corporation organized under the laws of the State of
Wyoming, acting by and through its political subdivision, the Cheyenne Police Department,
hereinafter referred to as the “Department,” and Leslie Burch, hereinafter referred to as “Burch.”
WfFNESSETH:
WHEREAS, the Department is a law enforcement agency serving the City of Cheyenne, and
is a department thereof; and
WHEREAS, the Department has received a grant of funds from the Wyoming Division of
Victim Services for the purpose of providing crime victim assistance services; and
WHEREAS, in order to provide crime victim assistance services, the Department desires to
retain the services of a “Victim Assistance Coordinator;” and
WHEREAS, because funding a Victim Assistance Coordinator position is dependent on the
receipt of a grant, the Department wishes to create a contract employee rather than permanent
employee position; and
WHEREAS, Burch has training and experience in the field of assisting crime victims; and
WHEREAS, Burch desires to provide services to the Department under the terms and
conditions hereinafter contained.
NOW, THEREFORE, in consideration of the promises and mutua] covenants herein, the
parties agree as follows:
1.
The term of this Agreement shall commence July 1, 2019, and terminate June 30,
2020, unless sooner terminated pursuant to Section 9 below or if grant funding is no longer available.
2.
Burch will be considered a contract employee of the Department. She will act as
Victim Assistance Coordinator and assist the Department.
3.
Burch shall at all times coordinate her activities hereunder with the Department and
shall work under the direction of the Department.
4.
The Department agrees to pay Burch the sum of Four Thousand Eight Dollars and
Twenty-One Cents ($4008.21) per month and longevity pay, not to exceed the amount of Sixty-Five
Dollars ($65.00) per month. The total amount over the term of this agreement will not, in any event,
exceed the sum of Forty-Eight Thousand Eight Hundred Seventy-Eight Dollars and Fifty-Two Cents
($48,878.52).
5.
The Department shall provide Burch the benefits provided to full-time employees of
the City of Cheyenne. The City of Cheyenne will withhold appropriate federal income and social
security taxes and remit them to the federal government.
6.
Tn addition to the compensation set forth above, the Department agrees to pay Burch
for hours worked in excess of forty hours in a work week at time and one-half rate.
7.
In the event that the governing body authorizes a bonus to be paid to city employees,
Burch would be eligible to receive a bonus similar to other city employees. Such bonus payment
shall first be made out of grant funds, if available, then out of Department funds, if grant funds are
not available.
1
```

### Page 2 of 2

```text
8.
Burch is subject to the City of Cheyenne Personnel Rules and Regulations, all federal
and state laws, city ordinances and actions of the city’s governing body pertaining generally to city
employees, except that Burch shall not be entitled to the procedural protections set forth in the
following sections ofthe City’s personnel rules: Chapter X, Section 3.C., last sentence; Chapter X,
Section 3.D.2; Chapter X, Section 3.D.3; Chapter XI; and Chapter XII, Section 2.B. and 2.C.
Because this contract is for one year and because the funding for the position is dependent on grant
funding, Burch is not a permanent employee ofthe City of Cheyenne. It is mutually understood and
agreed that Burch is employed on an “at will” basis and that her employment may be terminated by
the Department, with or without cause.
9.
This Agreement may be terminated by the Department, with or without cause.
10.
Burch agrees to comply with all applicable federal, state and local laws, rules and
regulations in the performance of this Agreement.
11.
Ifany provision, section, subsection, sentence, clause or phrase ofthis Agreement is
invalidated by any court of competent jurisdiction, the Agreement will automatically terminate.
12.
All parties acknowledge full opportunity for consultation with legal counsel regarding
this Agreement, or have consulted with legal counsel.
13.
The City of Cheyenne and the Department do not waive their sovereign inmiunity by
entering into this Agreement and fully retain all immunities and defenses provided by law in respect
to any action based on or occurring as a result of this Agreement.
14.
This Agreement contains the entire understanding of the parties. There are no other
terms or conditions, written or oral, concerning or controlling this matter. Time is of the essence
hereof
N WITNESS WHEREOF, the parties have hereunder set their hands and seals the day and
year first above written.
CITY OF CHEYENNE
